      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FNe6ccVXASyWnersKzl_f",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -20987.526729211786,
      "y": -24452.864910613596,
      "width": 1150.69921875,
      "height": 1200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 812815028,
      "version": 1376,
      "versionNonce": 552416684,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1766662780921,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements:-\n1. Appointment Management\nThe system shall allow patients to browse and select doctors.\nThe system shall allow patients to book appointments with selected doctors.\nThe system shall allow doctors to view their scheduled appointments.\n\n2. Patient Information Management\nThe system shall allow doctors to access and view information related to their patients.\nThe system shall maintain patient-related data associated with each doctor.\n\n3. Communication System\n- The system shall provide a chat feature to enable communication between patients and doctors.\n\n- Doctor–Medical Ai Service Data Exchange\n The interaction between doctors and the Medical AI Analysis Service is not a chat-based communication.\n Instead, it follows an asynchronous request–response model where doctors submit\n medical data for analysis, and the AI service processes the data and returns structured results.\n\n4. Chatbot Support\nThe system shall include a chatbot to assist users with general inquiries and platform usage.\n\nNon-Functional Requirements:-\n\n1- Security\nThe system shall enforce secure login and role-based access control.\nThe system shall ensure confidentiality and privacy of patient medical data.\n\n2- Reliability & Availability\nThe system shall ensure that essential services (appointment booking, data exchange, chat) are available at all times.\nThe system shall handle failures gracefully and preserve user data in case of errors.\n\n3- Usability\nThe system shall provide an intuitive and user-friendly interface for all user types.\nThe system shall be accessible via both web and mobile platforms.\n\n\nCore Entities:-\n1- User: UserID, Name, Email, Role(Patient/Doctor/Lab)\n2- Patient: PatientID, Personal Info, Medical Data\n3- Doctor: DoctorID, Specialty , Assigned Patients\n4- Medical AI Service : ServiceID ,ServiceType (Radiology, Blood Analysis, etc.) ,SupportedDataTypes\n5- Appointment: AppointmentID, Patient, Doctor, Data&Time, Status\n6- Medical Data: DataID, Data Type(image,report), sender(Doctor), Receiver(Lab)\n7- AI Analysis Result : ResultID, Confidence Score ,Findings ,Recommendations\n8- Chat: ChatID, Participants, Message\n9- Message: MessageID , Sender, content, Timestamp\n10- Chatbot: BotID, Knowledge Base\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements:-\n1. Appointment Management\nThe system shall allow patients to browse and select doctors.\nThe system shall allow patients to book appointments with selected doctors.\nThe system shall allow doctors to view their scheduled appointments.\n\n2. Patient Information Management\nThe system shall allow doctors to access and view information related to their patients.\nThe system shall maintain patient-related data associated with each doctor.\n\n3. Communication System\n- The system shall provide a chat feature to enable communication between patients and doctors.\n\n- Doctor–Medical Ai Service Data Exchange\n The interaction between doctors and the Medical AI Analysis Service is not a chat-based communication.\n Instead, it follows an asynchronous request–response model where doctors submit\n medical data for analysis, and the AI service processes the data and returns structured results.\n\n4. Chatbot Support\nThe system shall include a chatbot to assist users with general inquiries and platform usage.\n\nNon-Functional Requirements:-\n\n1- Security\nThe system shall enforce secure login and role-based access control.\nThe system shall ensure confidentiality and privacy of patient medical data.\n\n2- Reliability & Availability\nThe system shall ensure that essential services (appointment booking, data exchange, chat) are available at all times.\nThe system shall handle failures gracefully and preserve user data in case of errors.\n\n3- Usability\nThe system shall provide an intuitive and user-friendly interface for all user types.\nThe system shall be accessible via both web and mobile platforms.\n\n\nCore Entities:-\n1- User: UserID, Name, Email, Role(Patient/Doctor/Lab)\n2- Patient: PatientID, Personal Info, Medical Data\n3- Doctor: DoctorID, Specialty , Assigned Patients\n4- Medical AI Service : ServiceID ,ServiceType (Radiology, Blood Analysis, etc.) ,SupportedDataTypes\n5- Appointment: AppointmentID, Patient, Doctor, Data&Time, Status\n6- Medical Data: DataID, Data Type(image,report), sender(Doctor), Receiver(Lab)\n7- AI Analysis Result : ResultID, Confidence Score ,Findings ,Recommendations\n8- Chat: ChatID, Participants, Message\n9- Message: MessageID , Sender, content, Timestamp\n10- Chatbot: BotID, Knowledge Base\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "lqAxddVaiw-XQHUCsB6nS",
      "type": "freedraw",
      "x": -20736.900437524077,
      "y": -24440.317143710097,
      "width": 232.74010792915215,
      "height": 5.387502878947998,
